On 29 November 2020, members of the [[Peruvian Aprista Party]] chose a presidential ticket for the [[2021 Peruvian general election|2021 presidential election]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://resultadoshistorico.onpe.gob.pe/IN2020/Home|title=Elecciones Internas|date=29 November 2020|access-date=8 September 2025|website=ONPE}}</ref>

The party elected former cabinet minister [[Nidia Vílchez]] as the presidential nominee, defeating by a large margin the two other candidates, alongside her running mates Iván Hidalgo, former deputy minister of Social Development, and Olga Cribilleros, former [[Congress of the Republic of Peru|member of Congress]] from [[Department of La Libertad|La Libertad]].<ref>{{cite news|title=Elecciones 2021 &#124; Partido Aprista Peruano &#124; el Apra va a elecciones internas: Una estrella golpeada que busca la renovación &#124; POLITICA|url=https://elcomercio.pe/politica/elecciones/elecciones-2021-partido-aprista-peruano-el-apra-va-sus-elecciones-internas-con-animo-de-renovacion-noticia/|access-date=8 September 2025|work=El Comercio|date=27 November 2020|language=es-ES|quote=The APRA is preparing for this Sunday's internal elections, with three options for the presidential pre-candidacy.}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|title=Nidia Vílchez encabeza resultados de internas del Apra al 60.6% de actas contabilizadas|url=https://peru21.pe/politica/apra-nidia-vilchez-encabeza-resultados-de-elecciones-internas-al-606-de-actas-contabilizadas-elecciones-2021-nndc-noticia/|access-date=8 September 2025|work=Perú21|date=30 November 2020|language=es-ES|quote=Former Minister for Women Nidia Vilchez leads the results of the internal elections in the Peruvian Aprista Party with 60.6% of the votes counted, according to the National Office of Electoral Processes (ONPE).}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|title=Estos son los resultados de las elecciones internas de Acción Popular, Partido Morado y Apra a más del 90% de actas|url=https://diariocorreo.pe/politica/elecciones-2021-estos-son-los-resultados-de-las-internas-del-accion-popular-partido-morado-y-apra-a-mas-del-90-de-actas-nndc-noticia/|access-date=8 September 2025|work=Diario Correo|date=30 November 2020|language=es-ES|quote=Former Minister for Women Nidia Vílchez leads the results of the internal elections in the Peruvian Aprista Party with 93.61% of the votes counted, according to the National Office of Electoral Processes (ONPE).}}</ref>

Subsequently, the party withdrew her nomination once registered as a candidate at the [[National Jury of Elections]] after the party was denied registering their congressional candidates past the deadline.<ref>{{cite news|title=APRA retira su fórmula presidencial de las elecciones generales|url=https://larepublica.pe/elecciones/2021/01/16/el-apra-retira-su-formula-presidencial-de-las-elecciones-generales-pltc|access-date=8 September 2025|work=La República|date=15 January 2021|language=es-ES|quote=Presidential nominee [[Nidia Vílchez]] will be out of the electoral race after the JNE declares most of the lists of candidates for Congress inadmissible.}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|title=Elecciones 2021: Apra retira candidatura presidencial de Nidia Vílchez|url=https://andina.pe/agencia/noticia-elecciones-2021-apra-retira-candidatura-presidencial-nidia-vilchez-830046.aspx|access-date=8 September 2025|work=Andina Noticias|date=15 January 2021|language=es-ES|quote=The presidential ticket of the [[Peruvian Aprista Party]] (APRA), headed by [[Nidia Vílchez]], was withdrawn by decision of the party's political commission, confirmed the head of that body, [[Mauricio Mulder]].}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|title=Elecciones 2021: JEE de Lima Centro 1 aceptó el retiro de la plancha presidencial del Apra|url=https://diariocorreo.pe/politica/elecciones-2021-jee-de-lima-centro-1-acepto-el-retiro-de-la-plancha-presidencial-del-apra-nndc-noticia/|access-date=8 September 2025|work=Diario Correo|date=11 February 2021|language=es-ES|quote=The electoral authority accepted the Aprista Party's request to withdraw the presidential ticket headed by [[Nidia Vílchez]], after failing to register almost all of its parliamentary lists.}}</ref>

